[
    {
        "content": "<p>Simp lemmas <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.push_append_toArray#doc\">docs#List.push_append_toArray</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Array.append_singleton#doc\">docs#Array.append_singleton</a> are normalizing in opposite directions:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check_tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">append_singleton</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check_tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push_append_toArray</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In particular this makes normalization of arrays sensitive to the context and sensitive to the number of elements of an array in the context, resulting in terms that diverge rather than converge:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check_simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₃</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₃</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">~&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₃</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I ran into this expecting the following to close by simp:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Should <code>List.push_append_toArray</code> normalize in the opposite direction (cons → push)? It would close this goal.</p>",
        "id": 606589859,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1782421590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for the report. I have opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14208\">lean4#14208</a> to track this. It's likely that we'll address this as part of a larger effort to improve the <code>simp</code> set for <code>List</code> and <code>Array</code> (there are a number of interconnected open problems there).</p>",
        "id": 607066268,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1782712802
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span></p>",
        "id": 607749876,
        "sender_full_name": "Loren Abdulezer",
        "timestamp": 1782966069
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the update! FWIW I experimented with the change I suggested, there was not a lot of fallout in Lean itself but I didn't check for breakage elsewhere:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/frangio/lean4/commit/655d3d5c7e2a0eeb6f1da89224ad4dfe69ebbf6e\">https://github.com/frangio/lean4/commit/655d3d5c7e2a0eeb6f1da89224ad4dfe69ebbf6e</a></p>",
        "id": 607911724,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1783016695
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Meanwhile and in case others run into this, I'm just including this in my codebase:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push_append_toArray</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">append_toArray_cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">push_append_toArray</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
